\@writefile{loc}{\contentsline {deleted}{Deleted: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{ A teenager who occasionally encounters a Trump ``Fake News'' meme in a non-political group chat might chuckle and scroll on, while a committed partisan in a politicized TikTok bubble may interpret the same image as a rallying symbol or an unforgivable insult. From this perspective, partisan memes might function less as tools of mass persuasion and more as mechanisms for maintaining already polarized communities.}}{4}{section*.41}\protected@file@percent }
